---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

// Update this whenever the page below changes. A /now page that has
// clearly gone stale is worse than not having one.
const updated = 'September 18, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Now | Joe Fazio"
  description="What Joe Fazio is studying and building at the moment."
>
  <h1>Now</h1>
  <p class="meta">Last updated {updated}</p>

  <p>
    What I am studying and building at the moment. This page gets updated as
    things change rather than left to go stale.
  </p>

  <h2>Studying for CompTIA Security+</h2>

  <p>
    Security+ is an entry-level security certification covering network
    security, threat identification, access control and incident response. My
    coursework already covered the framework side of this, NIST CSF 2.0 and CIS
    Controls v8 on the <a href="/projects">BRHS risk assessment</a>. Security+
    is the structured version of the same material with an exam attached.
  </p>

  <h2>Next up: PowerShell automation</h2>

  <p>
    Scripts that handle real systems administration tasks: parsing log files,
    bulk user operations and scheduled health checks. I am already working in
    PowerShell daily to build and deploy this site, and these are the tasks that
    show up in the IT roles I am applying for, help desk and systems
    administration especially. They will go in a public repository as they are
    finished.
  </p>

  <h2>This site</h2>

  <p>
    Ongoing, and the best current example of how I work. Terraform for the
    Cloudflare configuration and a small Cloudflare Worker are the next pieces.
    <a href="/projects">The projects page</a> has the current state of it.
  </p>
</Layout>
